        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IVAtr">IV Atr</ref> Inscr.</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="IV Atr. Inscr." corresp="#wit-q">[Item rex Lundonie.]</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="la" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-q">[Item rex Lundoniae.] [R of Q]</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">[Ferner der König zu London.]</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">[Further, the king at London.]</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Latin only (Quadripartitus, after III Atr, Pax and Wal; from R, compared with TMHkBr). Heading only in R; ‘Lundonie’ probably stood in the archetype, perhaps in the heading or prologue of the lost Old English original. Dated c. 991–c. 1002.</note>
      </div>
